    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17555" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτάρ</span></b>  (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀϝυτάρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12.1012
				</span></i>
			), Conj. 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτάρ</span>
			 (
				Ep.
			 and <i><span class="en">Cypr.,
					<u>Inscr.Cypr.</u>57</span></i>
				H.):—<i>but, besides, moreover,</i> prop. to
			introduce a contrast, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				13.286
			</span></i>, al.; also to mark a rapid succession of details, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.406
			</span></i>, al.; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέν, Ἥφαιστος μέν . .
				αὐ. ἄρα Ζεύς</span> . . ib.<i><span class="en">
				102
			</span></i> sq., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.512
			</span></i> sq.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτάρ τοι</span>”
				<i>but nevertheless,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.45
				</span></i>
			.—In an Epic reminiscence, <i><span class="en">
				Hermipp.
				63.17
			</span></i> (hex.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτάρ: αὐτομάτη, ἑκουσία,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
